"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nFound in Godot v4.4.1-stable_win64\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 11, Hybrid Radeon integrated graphics (which are enabled for non-games by default) and RTX 3050 Ti Laptop edition, Forward+ rendering. My laptop is a Lenovo Ideapad Gaming 3 15ACH6.\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen creating a `Vector2` with `Vector2.from_angle()`, the `.length()` function doesn't always return `1.0`. Looks like a precision error, though it can be fixed by appending `.normalized()`.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nHere's my faulty code, it gets called every frame.\n\n```\nvar forward_vector = Vector2.from_angle(rotation)\nprint(\"NO FIX: %s\" % forward_vector.length())\nprint(\"W/ FIX: %s\" % forward_vector.normalized().length())\n```\n\nNote how the resultant `Vector2` is being printed once with and once without my band-aid fix.\n\nHere's an excerpt from my debugger:\n\n```\nGodot Engine v4.4.1.stable.official.49a5bc7b6 - https://godotengine.org\nVulkan 1.3.278 - Forward+ - Using Device #0: NVIDIA - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3050 Ti Laptop GPU\n\nNO FIX: 1.0\nW/ FIX: 1.0\nNO FIX: 0.99999994039536\nW/ FIX: 1.0\nNO FIX: 1.0\nW/ FIX: 1.0\nNO FIX: 0.99999994039536\nW/ FIX: 1.0\nNO FIX: 1.0\nW/ FIX: 1.0\nNO FIX: 0.99999994039536\nW/ FIX: 1.0\n--- Debugging process stopped ---\n```\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nHere's a project where a vector pointing towards the camera is constructed and displayed using `Vector2.to_angle()`.\n\n[vector2-bug-report - final.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19778061/vector2-bug-report.-.final.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"http